# .mailmap -- canonical author/email map for git shortlog and git blame
#
# Syntax (one entry per line, see gitmailmap(5)):
#
#   <proper-name> <proper-email>  <commit-name> <commit-email>
#   <proper-name> <proper-email>
#
# The first column is the "real" identity.  Subsequent columns are
# aliases that should be folded into the real one.  The file is
# applied bottom-up, so put the most specific entries first.
#
# Generated from `git log --format='%an <%ae>' | sort | uniq -c`,
# 2026-07-28.  Comments name the upstream variation that was
# unified; the actual project policy is "use the most recent
# canonical form for the canonical identity".

