# --- i18n bot accounts (treat as the same "author") ---

# mate-i18n is a script that commits translations on behalf of the
# project.  Attribute the script's commits to the maintainer who
# runs the import (Clement Lefebvre, in this case).  Translations
# coming in as a bot commit are translated in the GTK / GNOME
# infrastructure and dropped onto the Linux Mint maintainer's
# behalf.
Clement Lefebvre             <clement.lefebvre@linuxmint.com>  mate-i18n                    <mate-i18n@ml.mate-desktop.org>

# --- Forward-port author (the yuri-schmaltz fork's automation) ---

# Anything in the form 'Name <noreply>@users.noreply.github.com' that
# originates from a PR via the GitHub web UI is the human author
# (whose real name is in the surrounding commit message), not
# 'web-flow'.  Skip them here -- they are noise from the point of
# view of the real git shortlog, but the real identity is already
# in the original (non-noreply) commit author.
